  "answer": "All five writable files were rewritten; no other files were touched.\n\n**Changes**\n- `normalize.mjs`: `normalizeIssue` now builds a fresh object in order `id, title, tags, assignee` without mutating input. ID/title are trimmed (case preserved); tags are trimmed, lowercased, empties dropped, first-occurrence deduped in original order into a new array; assignee is trimmed+lowercased with empty → `null`, and `null` stays `null`. Validation still delegates to `assertIssue` (`TypeError('invalid issue')`).\n- `consumers/list.mjs`: no longer sorts or mutates the input array; validates array-ness (`TypeError('issues must be an array')`) and maps to normalized copies in input order (duplicate IDs preserved).\n- `consumers/search.mjs`: validates query string, uses `listIssues`, trims/lowercases the query, returns the whole normalized list for empty query, otherwise matches normalized title (case-insensitive) or any normalized tag; never matches id/assignee; fresh array per call.\n- `consumers/activity.mjs`: uses `listIssues`, renders `id|assignee|tags` with `-` for null assignee and comma-joined tags (empty tags → empty final field).\n- `serialize.mjs`: serializes `listIssues(issues)` so JSON matches list order and normalized property order, with no extra fields.\n\n`legacy.mjs`, `api.mjs`, fixtures, validators, and date/paging/console helpers were left unchanged, so `legacyTitle`, `boardSnapshot`, and unrelated exports keep their behavior.\n\n**Checked:** read all relevant sources and traced the spec examples by hand (e.g. `B-2` → `{id:'B-2',title:'Fix API',tags:['ui','backend'],assignee:'ada'}`, `X|-|a`, and the expected JSON string). No tests were executed — the environment provides no shell or test runner.",
